  "verdict": {
    "letter": "A",
    "text": "The run engine underweights starting-pitcher quality: its lambda edge moves only ~0.45 runs across the full observed SP-ERA-diff spectrum while actual home win rate swings ~7-8pp, so the derived ML inherits the compression and systematically overstates the home side in away-favored matchups. Directional big-SP evidence: home SP >=1.5 better actual 0.572 vs binary 0.560 vs derived 0.553; away SP >=1.5 better actual 0.484 vs binary 0.509 vs derived 0.514 \u2014 the binary tracks actuals more closely on both flanks. Live-card profile (away SP >=1.5 better, binary home 34-45%): away teams won 65.6% OOF; the binary's mean away prob was 57.9% (closer by 7.7%) while the derived ML mean was 54.5% (off by 11.1%). Verdict C is NOT supported: on OOF the binary's 60-65% home band is calibrated (actual ~61%) and its >65% band is under-confident (actual above prediction), the opposite of an overconfident high band. Verdict B's home level is present but calibrated: at lambda parity (|edge|<=0.3) derived sits at 0.530 vs actual 0.526, a flat ~53% home base rate produced by the documented tie-resolution constant MARGIN_PLUS1_HOME_SHARE=0.744 \u2014 structural, not spurious.",
    "recommended_action": "A: audit the run-engine side-model view's SP sensitivity (feature scaling/regularization of sp_era_* and the bullpen family); optionally label the derived-ML overlay that it embeds the calibrated home tie-resolution term and is NOT the binary moneyline."
  }
